What is AEM Dispatcher?
Definition: AEM Dispatcher is a caching and load-balancing tool that improves the performance, security and scalability of an AEM website.
In simple words, Dispatcher acts as a middle layer between users and the AEM Publish instance.
Real-time example:
Imagine 1,000 users visiting the same college website.
Without caching, every request reaches the AEM Publish server.
With Dispatcher, frequently requested pages are served from the cache.
This reduces the load on the Publish server and improves response time.


2. Main functions of Dispatcher
Caching: Stores frequently accessed website pages.
Load Balancing: Distributes requests across multiple Publish instances.
Filtering: Blocks unwanted or unauthorized requests.
Security: Helps protect AEM from direct external access.
Cache Invalidation: Ensures outdated cached content is refreshed.
